    "finalName": "",
    "description": "Whenever you make a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Stealth\" title=\"Stealth\">Stealth</a> check to <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Sneak\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Sneak\">Sneak</a>, you can use your check result in place of one adjacent ally's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Stealth\" title=\"Stealth\">Stealth</a> check to <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Sneak\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Sneak\">Sneak</a> (additionally, if you have the <b>Force Immersion</b> Talent, that Talent applies to the designated ally as well).<br><br>Similarly, you can use your <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Use_the_Force\" title=\"Use the Force\">Use the Force</a> check result in the place of an adjacent ally's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Use_the_Force\" title=\"Use the Force\">Use the Force</a> check result to avoid detection by the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Sense_Force\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Sense Force\">Sense Force</a> application of the skill. You can spend a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Force_Point\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Force Point\">Force Point</a> to have this ability apply to all adjacent allies instead of just one.",
